.TH OCR-SHOT 1 "August 2026" "ocr-shot 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocr-shot \- Live Text OCR screenshot utility for Void Linux (Wayland & X11)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocr-shot
[\fILANGUAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-gui\fR] [\fB\-\-cli\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocr-shot
captures a screen region and interactively extracts text using Tesseract OCR, featuring an Apple Live Text-like visual overlay. Supports multi-language combined scans (Indonesian, English, Arabic) and works under both Wayland and X11 sessions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I LANGUAGE
Target OCR language code(s) separated by '+' (e.g., \fBind+eng+ara\fR, \fBind\fR, \fBeng\fR, \fBara\fR). Default is \fBind+eng+ara\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Force interactive GUI Live Text overlay mode.
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Force non-interactive CLI mode (copies detected text directly to system clipboard).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Export full text and word bounding box coordinates (x, y, w, h) in structured JSON format.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInteractive Overlay\fR: Screen freeze with word bounding box highlights, click-and-drag text selection, double-click word selection, and triple-click line selection.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSmart Data Detectors\fR: Automatically detects URLs (\fBOpen Link\fR), Email addresses (\fBSend Email\fR), Phone numbers (\fBCall/Copy Phone\fR), and Physical Locations (\fBGoogle Maps\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSelect All Shortcut\fR: Press \fBCtrl+A\fR or click \fBAll\fR to select all detected text instantly.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBContext Menu\fR: Right-click anywhere on selection for quick action context menu.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBParagraph Join Mode\fR: Toggle between raw line breaks and unified paragraph text formatting.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBToast Notifications\fR: Visual feedback upon copying text.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/ocr-shot/config.json
Optional user configuration file to customize default settings.
